# VY-TermWEB service configuration
#
# RUN_AS_USER (required): existing system user the server runs as.
# The web UI exposes a local PTY shell and a filesystem browser with no
# authentication — whoever can reach the port gets a shell as this user.
# The installer pre-fills this with the user who ran `sudo dpkg -i`.
RUN_AS_USER=

# PORT: HTTP port (default 32230)
#PORT=32230

# SHELL: shell used for Local Shell sessions (default: the user's login shell)
#SHELL=/bin/bash

# VY_MASTER_PASSWORD: master password gating the whole web panel (terminals,
# files and tools). Uncomment to require a password — without it the panel is
# open to anyone who can reach the port. Stored here in plaintext, so this
# file is installed root-readable only (0600). Alternative: leave unset and
# create the password on the first web access (stored as PBKDF2 hash in
# ~/.vy-termweb/auth.json of RUN_AS_USER).
#VY_MASTER_PASSWORD=

# VY_AUTH_DISABLED=1: disable the panel password entirely (not recommended —
# the UI has no other protection; use only behind a VPN/auth proxy or on
# loopback-only setups).
#VY_AUTH_DISABLED=
